  "findings": [
    "Inventory, quality, desktop build, plugin renderer, and loaded-plugin workflows passed; Rust CI and the pinned Obsidian 1.14.4 vault round-trip failed on all required jobs.",
    "Rust CI workspace tests failed the same four existing egui note-selector tests on Ubuntu, macOS, Windows, and Rust 1.95: each selection remained README.md. Ubuntu also reported rustfmt differences in crates/engine/src/lib.rs, crates/ui-egui/src/lib.rs, and crates/vault/src/lib.rs.",
    "The four selector tests were egui_invalid_utf8_note_preview_fails_closed_without_changing_vault_or_app_data, egui_note_inspect_combobox_disambiguates_duplicate_basenames_without_writes, egui_note_inspect_combobox_preserves_unicode_and_spaced_paths_without_writes, and egui_note_inspect_combobox_selects_a_note_and_clears_previews_without_writes. Each affected test job reported 105 passed and 4 failed.",
    "The new Canvas editor header displaced the existing note selector in the native UI. The correction moves that header after the existing panels.",
    "The round-trip reached the Canvas editing UI but stopped before Save on all three operating systems. Linux OCR misread the text-card label; Windows OCR missed the disabled Save label although the draft loaded; macOS could not find the hyphenated text-card field label through AX or OCR. The vault remained unchanged and no note was created.",
    "The correction applies OCR-tolerant field-label recognition, checks the explicit Canvas text loaded status rather than OCR of the disabled Save label, and accepts hyphenated-label OCR tokenization variants."
  ],
  "local_validation": "No local tests, builds, formatters, linters, validators, or application launches were run. Round-trip archives were inspected for CI evidence only. One accidental local `git diff --check` during source inspection returned clean; it was a local whitespace check and is recorded as a process deviation. Subsequent formatting corrections apply the exact diff printed by GitHub Actions; formatter execution remains reserved for CI."
